          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What TSH range does guidance describe as the treatment threshold in subclinical hypothyroidism?",
          "answer": "I could not find a TSH treatment threshold in the guidance I searched. The retrieved passage from the hypothyroidism guidance (\"Hypothyroidism: which test comes first, and the monitoring interval after a change,\" an endocrinology and thyroid association educational summary) explains how subclinical hypothyroidism is defined. It is a raised TSH with free thyroxine still within the reference range. It also says thyroid peroxidase antibodies help estimate how likely subclinical disease is to progress. But it does not state a TSH number at which treatment is recommended.\n\nThe passage that would normally cover this, on when treatment starts, was not among the results. I can't fill that gap from general knowledge. A clinician or the full version of that guidance document can give the specific threshold and how it is applied.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
